1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:01,680
You wake up tomorrow morning.

2
00:00:01,700 --> 00:00:03,120
Your alarm is ringing.

3
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:05,400
Sunlight is coming through your window.

4
00:00:05,420 --> 00:00:07,760
Everything seems completely normal.

5
00:00:07,780 --> 00:00:10,040
Until you check your phone.

6
00:00:10,060 --> 00:00:11,240
No new messages.

7
00:00:11,260 --> 00:00:12,580
No missed calls.

8
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:14,720
Nobody has posted anything.

9
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:16,260
You call your best friend.

10
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:17,180
Nothing.

11
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:18,620
You call your family.

12
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:19,680
Nothing.

13
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:21,140
You step outside.

14
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:24,820
The streets are empty.

15
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:27,200
Cars sit abandoned along the road.

16
00:00:27,220 --> 00:00:30,280
The shops are open, but nobody is inside.

17
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:34,420
And slowly, a terrifying
possibility enters your mind.

18
00:00:35,279 --> 00:00:37,920
What if you're the last human being alive?

19
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:41,100
At first, you don't believe it.

20
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:44,360
You search houses,
hospitals, police stations.

21
00:00:44,380 --> 00:00:47,780
You drive through neighbourhoods,
shouting for someone to answer.

22
00:00:48,220 --> 00:00:49,760
But nobody does.

23
00:00:50,740 --> 00:00:52,160
And the strangest part?

24
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:53,880
The world hasn't ended.

25
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:55,620
Electricity is still running.

26
00:00:55,640 --> 00:00:57,460
Water still comes from the tap.

27
00:00:57,480 --> 00:00:59,900
The internet might even work for a while.

28
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:01,660
Humanity has vanished.

29
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:04,380
But the machines it built
haven't stopped yet.

30
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:06,220
So what happens next?

31
00:01:07,640 --> 00:01:12,460
During your first twenty-four hours, survival
might actually be surprisingly easy.

32
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:14,260
Supermarkets are full of food.

33
00:01:14,280 --> 00:01:15,960
Petrol stations have fuel.

34
00:01:15,980 --> 00:01:18,180
Homes are stocked with supplies.

35
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,020
You could sleep in a mansion,
drive an expensive car,

36
00:01:21,040 --> 00:01:23,820
or walk through a museum
without buying a ticket.

37
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:25,540
But there's a problem.

38
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:30,100
Almost everything you rely on was designed
to be maintained by other people.

39
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:32,600
And those people are gone.

40
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:37,940
As the hours pass, electricity
networks begin facing problems.

41
00:01:37,960 --> 00:01:41,360
Power plants and substations
depend on automated controls,

42
00:01:41,380 --> 00:01:46,640
but also on operators, fuel deliveries,
maintenance and a functioning grid.

43
00:01:46,660 --> 00:01:49,000
Some facilities would shut down safely.

44
00:01:49,020 --> 00:01:51,080
Others could experience faults.

45
00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:53,980
Different areas would lose
power at different times.

46
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,700
There's no single moment when
every light on Earth switches off.

47
00:01:58,160 --> 00:02:01,380
But eventually, your
neighbourhood could go dark.

48
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:05,060
And when the electricity
fails, your problems multiply.

49
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:06,960
Refrigerators stop cooling.

50
00:02:06,980 --> 00:02:09,160
Mobile networks lose backup power.

51
00:02:09,180 --> 00:02:10,740
Water pumps may stop.

52
00:02:10,760 --> 00:02:13,040
Wastewater systems begin failing.

53
00:02:13,060 --> 00:02:15,000
Your phone is still in your hand.

54
00:02:15,460 --> 00:02:17,340
But there's nobody left to call.

55
00:02:18,580 --> 00:02:21,640
By the end of the first
week, you need a plan.

56
00:02:21,660 --> 00:02:23,620
Fresh food is beginning to spoil.

57
00:02:23,640 --> 00:02:27,820
Depending on local infrastructure,
tap water may no longer be reliable.

58
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:31,020
You need bottled water,
preserved food, medicine,

59
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:33,880
warm clothing and a safe place to live.

60
00:02:33,900 --> 00:02:37,160
And you need to think about
something people rarely consider.

61
00:02:38,140 --> 00:02:39,060
Fire.

62
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:44,000
Without firefighters, a small blaze could
spread through an abandoned building.

63
00:02:44,020 --> 00:02:48,380
Without emergency services, even a
minor injury could become dangerous.

64
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:53,040
A broken ankle, an infected cut, or a
serious illness could leave you completely

65
00:02:53,060 --> 00:02:54,100
helpless.

66
00:02:55,380 --> 00:02:58,620
So you stop treating the world
like your personal playground.

67
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:01,340
And start treating it
like a survival problem.

68
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:05,500
You find a house with a fireplace, a
reliable water source and room to store

69
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:06,580
supplies.

70
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:10,900
You collect batteries, solar panels,
tools and first-aid equipment.

71
00:03:10,920 --> 00:03:13,940
You learn how to purify
water and preserve food.

72
00:03:15,180 --> 00:03:19,000
But while you're learning to survive,
something else is happening.

73
00:03:19,020 --> 00:03:21,880
Nature is beginning to reclaim the world.

74
00:03:21,900 --> 00:03:24,720
With traffic gone, roads become silent.

75
00:03:24,740 --> 00:03:29,000
Without constant human activity, many
animals begin exploring places they once

76
00:03:29,020 --> 00:03:30,040
avoided.

77
00:03:30,060 --> 00:03:32,220
Weeds push through pavement cracks.

78
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:34,180
Gardens become overgrown.

79
00:03:34,200 --> 00:03:37,160
Unmaintained buildings slowly deteriorate.

80
00:03:37,180 --> 00:03:39,960
But cities wouldn't turn
into forests overnight.

81
00:03:39,980 --> 00:03:42,180
Nature works on its own timescale.

82
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:45,680
And some of the most dramatic
changes would take decades.

83
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:51,680
Meanwhile, the animals humanity left
behind face very different futures.

84
00:03:51,700 --> 00:03:55,080
Some pets would struggle
without food, water or care.

85
00:03:55,100 --> 00:03:57,200
Others might escape and adapt.

86
00:03:57,220 --> 00:04:01,720
Livestock trapped in buildings or fenced
areas could be especially vulnerable.

87
00:04:01,740 --> 00:04:05,320
Wild animals, however, might benefit
from the disappearance of hunting,

88
00:04:05,340 --> 00:04:07,520
traffic and habitat disturbance.

89
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:09,900
The planet would continue changing.

90
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:11,720
Even without us.

91
00:04:12,820 --> 00:04:17,020
After one month, your biggest
enemy might no longer be hunger.

92
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:19,560
It might be loneliness.

93
00:04:19,580 --> 00:04:21,960
Humans evolved as social creatures.

94
00:04:21,980 --> 00:04:26,780
We depend on conversation,
cooperation, friendship and belonging.

95
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:30,760
Now imagine going thirty days
without hearing another human voice.

96
00:04:30,780 --> 00:04:31,740
No jokes.

97
00:04:31,760 --> 00:04:32,840
No arguments.

98
00:04:32,860 --> 00:04:34,440
No conversations.

99
00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:36,160
Nobody to celebrate with.

100
00:04:36,180 --> 00:04:39,320
Nobody to tell you that
everything is going to be okay.

101
00:04:39,340 --> 00:04:41,320
You might begin talking to yourself.

102
00:04:41,340 --> 00:04:42,720
Recording messages.

103
00:04:42,740 --> 00:04:45,820
Playing old videos just
to hear somebody speak.

104
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:50,020
And the longer you're alone, the harder it
could become to maintain motivation and a

105
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:51,620
normal daily routine.

106
00:04:51,640 --> 00:04:55,340
Because surviving physically
isn't the same as living well.

107
00:04:56,680 --> 00:04:58,520
So you create a schedule.

108
00:04:58,540 --> 00:05:01,060
You wake up at the same time every day.

109
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:04,920
You exercise, cook, repair
equipment and keep a journal.

110
00:05:04,940 --> 00:05:08,980
You search libraries for books on
farming, medicine and engineering.

111
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:11,800
And you keep looking for other survivors.

112
00:05:11,820 --> 00:05:14,560
Not because you've found
evidence that anyone remains.

113
00:05:14,580 --> 00:05:18,920
But because accepting that you're alone
forever might be the hardest part.

114
00:05:20,280 --> 00:05:23,280
One year later, the world
looks very different.

115
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:25,700
Many roads are damaged or obstructed.

116
00:05:25,720 --> 00:05:29,100
Buildings have suffered leaks,
weather damage and neglect.

117
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:31,900
Some areas have experienced
fires or flooding.

118
00:05:31,920 --> 00:05:35,480
And the technologies that once made
everyday life effortless are becoming

119
00:05:35,500 --> 00:05:37,720
increasingly difficult to use.

120
00:05:37,740 --> 00:05:40,500
You might still generate
electricity using solar panels,

121
00:05:40,520 --> 00:05:43,140
provided the equipment works
and you can maintain it.

122
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:46,640
You might grow vegetables, collect
rainwater and preserve food.

123
00:05:46,660 --> 00:05:48,840
But everything takes effort.

124
00:05:48,860 --> 00:05:51,480
Every repair is your responsibility.

125
00:05:51,500 --> 00:05:54,100
Every mistake is yours to solve.

126
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:58,260
And there's one final
reality you can't escape.

127
00:05:58,280 --> 00:06:01,400
If you truly are the last
human being on Earth,

128
00:06:01,420 --> 00:06:04,240
humanity has no future generation.

129
00:06:04,700 --> 00:06:07,720
When you die, the human story ends.

130
00:06:07,740 --> 00:06:12,800
Our cities, our music, our inventions and
our history would remain for a while.

131
00:06:12,820 --> 00:06:17,580
But without people to preserve them, much
of what we created would slowly disappear.

132
00:06:18,880 --> 00:06:21,240
Yet Earth itself would survive.

133
00:06:21,260 --> 00:06:22,620
Forests would grow.

134
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:24,040
Oceans would move.

135
00:06:24,060 --> 00:06:25,620
Animals would evolve.

136
00:06:25,640 --> 00:06:28,520
The planet doesn't need
humanity to keep spinning.

137
00:06:28,540 --> 00:06:32,680
But humanity needs something that no
amount of technology can replace.

138
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:34,960
Other humans.

139
00:06:35,900 --> 00:06:40,440
So if you woke up tomorrow and discovered
that everyone else had vanished...

140
00:06:40,860 --> 00:06:43,080
How long do you think you would survive?
